course: dictionary
lesson: 6874
title: Overland: travelling on land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «After about 1500 more trade between Europe and Asia went by sea, because ships could carry far more goods more cheaply, so the overland Silk Road became less important.» Look at the clues: the sentence says trade went by sea, and it contrasts that with the Silk Road. So overland must mean the opposite of by sea.
explain: Overland means across land, by road or on foot. It can be an adverb, as in «They travelled overland», or an adjective, as in «an overland route». Ask yourself: did the journey go over water or through the air? If not, it was probably overland.
explain: Historians and geographers use this word for long journeys. Pioneers went overland by wagon across America, and explorers crossed Australia overland. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «The pioneers went by land, by wagon» still makes sense.
fact: Overland means across land, by road or on foot.
fact: Overland can be an adverb («travelled overland») or an adjective («an overland route»).
fact: The opposite idea is travel by sea or by air.
fact: «Overland» tells you the journey went across land, as in «pioneers travelling overland by wagon».
fact: The Silk Road was an overland trade route, and it became less important when ships carried goods by sea.
exercise: «After about 1500 more trade between Europe and Asia went by sea, so the overland Silk Road became less important.» What does overland mean here? | Up in the air, by plane | By sea in big ships | Under the water | *Across land, by road or on foot
exercise: «The pioneers travelled overland by wagon across America.» Did the pioneers cross the sea? | Yes, they flew in planes | They travelled under the ground | Yes, they sailed in boats | *No, they travelled across land
exercise: «The explorers crossed Australia ___, on foot and by cart.» Which word fits the gap? | *overland | upwards | underwater | sideways
test: Which phrase describes a trip by road rather than by sea? | a swim in the lake | a voyage across the ocean | *an overland journey | a flight to the moon
test: Why did the overland Silk Road become less important after 1500? | Everyone stopped travelling | The road was flooded | *Ships could carry more goods more cheaply, so trade went by sea | Nobody wanted goods any more
exam: Which word means across land, by road or on foot, not by sea or air? | *overland | underground | overhead | overseas
